Caliptra's testbench services declare read_line with a ref argument and no
lifetime, in a module that gives none, so the function is static (IEEE
1800-2023 13.4.2). 13.5.2 says "It shall be illegal to use argument passing by
reference for subroutines with a lifetime of static". Declare it automatic;
each call sets every local before reading it, so the behavior is the same.

The text is Caliptra's own, reported as
https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-rtl/issues/1440 and fixed there in
https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-rtl/pull/1441. Sent to the suite as
https://github.com/verilator/rtlmeter/pull/61

--- a/designs/Caliptra/src/caliptra-rtl/caliptra_top_tb_services.sv
+++ b/designs/Caliptra/src/caliptra-rtl/caliptra_top_tb_services.sv
@@ -3219 +3219 @@
-function void read_line(int fd, int bit_length_words, ref bit [31:0] array []);
+function automatic void read_line(int fd, int bit_length_words, ref bit [31:0] array []);
